 "structural_change": "KVJ-A3 r2 HOST cluster child qkd_hr_core_peer (core family, one ck_core entry): members u_peer, u_peer_codec, u_root_mux, u_coordinator, u_ctrl + their glue, generated wrapper (tools/qwen_kv_die/host_cluster/gen_cluster.py). Partition results/arch/qwen_split_1014/host_root_cluster/partition_r2.json | r3 (KV-HROOT-PEER 10-18, gate ca25bcce7 FAIL: TT spread 80.6, insertion 472.7 from a NW-corner clock entry, reg->reg -272.8 (step_slot rank-0 RX / last_allocation TX), por_n 5,341 + host_rst_n 3,419 reset loads from the ports, util 17%): (a) every reset pin of the 5 members behind a local ot_rst_relay (tools/qwen_kv_die/host_cluster/gen_peer_rr.py; +3 release uniform); (b) root mux -> qkd_host_peer_root_mux_pl: cycle-exact one-hot TX round robin (no 512-b runtime part-select) + registered rank-0 RX slice (+1 cycle on rank0->coordinator class9 words; bench rtl/test/qwen_host/hr_peer_pl_1018); (c) outline 302.4 -> 280.8 (pin-bound: 6,301 pins, faces 5.5-5.8 /um after moving cd S, guarded_tk/slice_boot_done/step tags W, slice_boot_ok/seen/peer acks E), ck_core at the N-face centre (was the NW corner). | r4 (HKV-PROMPT6 10-19, routed r3-40d82161e NEEDS_RTL TT -174.78 / FF -11.03; routed sign-off STA classified: no reset-pin path among violators): (1) TT u_ctrl.u_m rp -> 4:1x512 head mux q[rp] -> h[511:K]==0 OR trees -> accept -> 744-flop tk8 / kst8 enable (all 400 listed endpoints, -174.8): registered queue head h (+ same-edge write forwarding) with zero flags computed at queue write (qkd_host_ctrl_token_service_packet_collected_pd, gen_peer_pd.py; bit/cycle exact, 0 cycles); (2) FF input pin-reg hold slice_boot_done/guarded_tk/step*_client_tag/cq_pos (-11.0, 150+ ep): route.io_hold_margin_ns 0.03; internal participant_trace -5.9 to route hold repair; (3) main RESET-LANDING: reset_landing 2 stages on por_n/host_rst_n ahead of the member relays (release +2 more ck_core edges, uniform). MU (allocator_mu) NOT carried: not wireable alone (MU-ADOPT-HROOT). | r5 (KV-PEER5 / REFILL-1330 10-19, SAFE-AUDIT-KV: r4 ec2f20a5f not submitted, checklist fails 3/4/7; r4 gate --cts TT placement reg->reg classes from a placement-RC STA of the r4 4_1_cts.odb: engine_result_v pin flop -> lifecycle selected-terminal compare -> lifecycle_fault -146.8 / terminal_* -133.2, local_service_epoch pin flop -> rank codec status -> root mux lq_d -97.0 / last_status -84.2, ctrl h -> tk8 -68.7, grant_position -> codec TX -> root mux / rank codec -68.4..-52.2, peer link pr -> physical RX -> coordinator RX -56.2): (1) CLOCK: ck_core pinned to the N-face centre (pin_ranges 136.8-144.0; r4 placed it at the NW end); (2) RESET COPIES: every member relay is ot_rst_relay #(REGIONS K) (coordinator por_n 28, ctrl rst_n 12 / por_n 1, peer link rst_n 7, rank codec por_n 16, root mux por_n 3; sized from the pre-optimisation async loads the hook counts: 6,532 / 2,732 / 58 / 1,596 / 3,624 / 536 -> <= 234 a copy) and synthesis spreads each member's async-reset flops over the K kept copies (physical/common_flow/ot_rst_split.tcl via orfs_vars OT_RST_SPLIT=1; error above 256 a copy; r4 had 5,165 / 2,165 / 1,260 / 893 on one flop); KV-RELAYGEN had not landed, so the copies are emitted here by gen_peer_rr.py the same way; (3) ROOT MUX r5 = qkd_host_peer_root_mux_pl2: REGISTERED ONE-HOT TX grant (ready from registers only, AND-OR load, no runtime part-select / wide shifter; +<=1 edge), TX rank-0 slice (+1), physical RX slice (+1), r3 rank-0 RX slice kept (bench rtl/test/qwen_host/hr_peer_pl2_1019, per-channel word streams vs the unchanged mux + fault parity); (4) INPUT STAGES (+1 edge, plain registers in the member wrappers): coordinator engine_result_* and rank codec status inputs (service/program/drain levels) (bench rtl/test/qwen_host/hr_peer_stage_1019, lock-step vs the member with the inputs delayed one edge); (5) ctrl _pd fork: the 13 runtime part-select writes X[role|src*W+:W] (tk8 93 b, kst8, boot8, service_epoch8, seq_rx) as constant-index one-hot slice writes (bit/cycle exact, peer_pd_equiv); (6) pin regs on, reset_landing 2, io_hold_margin 0.03 (unchanged from r4); util waiver: pin-bound (fill_reason). Added cycles -> KV static schedule / HOST calendar (class9 lifecycle transport, not the per-token compute schedule): coordinator<->rank TX/RX +1 each direction, engine result +1, rank-0 status +1.",
